update public.questions q
set explanation = v.e
from (values
('90d6e8d3-1039-41da-bc8d-a07582e8c850', '25^(1/2) is the square root of 25, so it equals 5 because 5 × 5 = 25. The 12.5 option is 25 ÷ 2, which confuses a power of one half with halving.'),
('90ef9b98-a49b-42f1-b1c8-9e1a08373314', 'In the worst case every key collides into the same bucket, so a lookup must check all n entries: O(n). Good hashing gives average O(1), but this question asks for the worst case.'),
('9101f57c-9521-41da-93a2-6d7bcc133e00', 'Newton''s second law gives F = ma = 2000 kg × 3 m s⁻² = 6000 N. The 667 N option is m ÷ a, which inverts the relationship.'),
('9108585b-c56c-4191-a971-f22ff0840db9', 'Use sin(A + B) = sin A cos B + cos A sin B with A = 45° and B = 30°. This gives (√2/2)(√3/2) + (√2/2)(1/2) = (√6 + √2)/4.'),
('9131edf6-bc62-4e89-a3f9-5e778d83768c', 'Heat energy is Q = mcΔT = 2 kg × 400 J kg⁻¹ K⁻¹ × 50 K = 40 000 J. A temperature change is a difference, so the 50 K can be used directly.'),
('917e60a6-0871-413c-bd70-ed8dae7772a9', 'The hex digit A is 10, and the 1 in the sixteens place is worth 16, so 1A = 1 × 16 + 10 = 26. The 16 option counts only the place value of the 1.'),
('91b4f0bc-07f4-495d-95d6-4cd9ef5038ef', 'For a binomial distribution Var(X) = np(1 − p). With n = 10 and p = 0.4 this gives 10 × 0.4 × 0.6 = 2.4. The 0.24 option is p(1 − p) without multiplying by n.'),
('92878e89-3c4b-4bb2-a5f7-9a42bea0638a', 'When complex numbers are multiplied in modulus–argument form, the moduli multiply and the arguments add. Division works the other way round, with moduli divided and arguments subtracted.'),
('93cdf801-52ec-4518-8bcf-a77698557063', 'An array stores its items in consecutive memory, so the address of item i is found by a direct calculation from the base address. Access takes the same time whatever the index, which is O(1).'),
('94063359-458c-42f1-a3a6-86b8b2172190', 'Write 3 sin x + 4 cos x = R sin(x + α) with R = √(3² + 4²) = 5. Since sin takes values up to 1, the maximum is R = 5, reached when sin(x + α) = 1.'),
('94275389-d8b5-45d8-a554-5e01be3d6528', 'In the stored-program concept, instructions and data are both held in main memory, and the processor fetches its instructions from there. This is the core idea of the von Neumann architecture.'),
('94b5bc57-a8cf-46e0-9456-fc7bbeac1960', 'Vectors are parallel when one is a scalar multiple of the other. Here (−2, 1) = −½ × (4, −2), so they are parallel. Their dot product is −10, not zero, so they are not perpendicular.'),
('9733d625-3fb7-4bc9-b420-7bd4fa5cb12c', 'The area of a circle is A = πr². With r = 3, A = π × 3² = 9π. The 3π option uses r rather than r².'),
('9806de5e-95de-448d-a2c5-bf099a3a2dc2', 'With J = K = 1 a JK flip-flop toggles: each clock pulse changes Q to its opposite. This removes the invalid S = R = 1 input of the SR flip-flop, which is the improvement JK offers.'),
('9875e8ee-f54f-4f8f-be8a-7661de469e25', 'Ohm''s law gives V = IR = 2 A × 6 Ω = 12 V. The 0.33 option is R ÷ I, which is not a voltage relationship.'),
('9948e822-6df5-485a-a405-f1c5c5a98cb6', 'The denominator x − 2 cannot be zero, because division by zero is undefined. The domain is every real number except x = 2, written x ≠ 2.'),
('9a65b29d-aa78-49a2-8cc0-365555ebd1bd', 'The Sun radiates about 3.9 × 10²⁶ W, which is the standard value of its luminosity. The 1370 W option is the solar constant, an intensity at Earth rather than the total power output.'),
('9ac9e96f-0ba6-4ca7-830c-0ecd80dbb02e', 'File size is samples per second × bits per sample × duration. Doubling the sampling rate doubles the number of samples, so the file size doubles.'),
('9ae917e3-c894-4640-9836-0c5d41488e6e', 'For 1 + i the real and imaginary parts are both 1, so tan θ = 1. The point lies in the first quadrant, so arg(1 + i) = tan⁻¹(1) = π/4.'),
('9b8a7a73-380e-4367-b9dd-98084a543f13', 'Parallel lines have the same gradient, so m₁ = m₂. The perpendicular condition is m₁ × m₂ = −1, which is a different relationship.'),
('9c02b870-a1fc-47f2-a7a0-fb9f3409189f', 'At the top of the flight v = 0, so 0 = u − gt gives t = u/g = 15 ÷ 9.81 ≈ 1.53 s. The 3.06 s option is the total time to return to the ground.'),
('9ce8853d-70b1-41b9-8b89-60d72ea70628', 'All electromagnetic waves travel at the same speed in a vacuum, c = 3.0 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹, whatever their frequency. Frequency affects only the wavelength in a given medium.'),
('9d5e8c6f-8c94-42e7-a68c-8b23dcbb6aff', 'Angular frequency is ω = 2π ÷ T = 2π ÷ 2.0 = π rad s⁻¹. The radius of 0.40 m is not needed for angular frequency.'),
('9ecfffbb-0a7e-403b-a1b4-c6c4c5a47689', 'A layer-2 switch reads the destination MAC address in each frame and forwards it out of the matching port. Port numbers belong to layer 4 and IP addresses to layer 3.'),
('9f2dcff7-1920-4a64-ad4b-2e0811a65f0a', '∫₀³ 2x dx = [x²]₀³ = 3² − 0² = 9. The power rule raises the index by one, and the coefficient 2 cancels against the division.'),
('9f411662-0b46-4426-b6d7-d3013073d015', 'A normal distribution is symmetric about its mean μ, so half the probability lies below μ: P(X < μ) = 0.5. The 0.3413 option is the probability between μ and μ + σ.'),
('a0bcaad0-903a-4329-8ac1-b549030231c0', 'For a uniform field between parallel plates, E = V ÷ d = 100 V ÷ 0.02 m = 5000 V m⁻¹. The 2 V/m option is V × d, the product rather than the quotient.'),
('a14e5d9a-ec48-45eb-b50d-60ac4bb4e212', 'To convert Celsius to kelvin add 273, so T = 25 + 273 = 298 K. The kelvin degree is the same size as the Celsius degree, but its zero is at absolute zero.'),
('a1a96016-534c-4f36-8d77-62b538d0aa1e', 'For y = A sin(bx) the amplitude is the coefficient A of the sine term, so the amplitude is 3. The 2 inside sin(2x) changes the period, not the amplitude.'),
('a27b0df5-b768-48be-9f23-fe4a67d6c904', 'Adding a constant c to every value shifts the whole distribution, so the mean increases by c. Here the mean increases by 5, and the spread of the data is unchanged.'),
('a2e4f793-8458-4487-83f0-d4dcd9111fb3', 'The mean is the sum of the values divided by how many there are: 40 ÷ 5 = 8. The 10 option is 40 ÷ 4, which divides by the wrong count.'),
('a31c3001-756a-4d42-8f7c-85697fa27872', 'Ohm''s law gives R = V ÷ I = 12 V ÷ 3 A = 4 Ω. The 36 ohm option is V × I, the product rather than the quotient.'),
('a32aec58-ab2d-4de3-86f2-04b8c43a7ede', 'Parallel wires send several bits at once. Over long distances the bits can drift out of alignment (skew), and neighbouring wires interfere (crosstalk). Serial transmission avoids both problems over long distances.'),
('a3639c83-cdc6-4a4c-a4d2-a406dd642099', 'Electrical power is P = VI = 230 V × 0.5 A = 115 W. The 460 W option is 230 × 2, which doubles the current by mistake.'),
('a37c78b9-aed6-4aa4-b1e8-4828e4d635d1', 'On a displacement–time graph the gradient is the rate of change of displacement, which is velocity. Acceleration is the gradient of a velocity–time graph, a different graph.'),
('a4640ef3-216f-4a76-98b4-9a53a56ff871', 'tan θ = opposite ÷ adjacent = 8 ÷ 6 = 4/3. The 6/8 option swaps the opposite and adjacent sides, which gives cot θ rather than tan θ.'),
('a4afa7fb-93a5-4dfc-a7e6-499e53b89a18', 'Momentum is p = mv = 2 kg × 6 m s⁻¹ = 12 kg m s⁻¹. The 3 kg m s⁻¹ option divides the velocity by the mass instead of multiplying.'),
('a5176007-4493-439d-a730-1904940850da', 'SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol) is the application-layer protocol used to send email between mail servers. FTP transfers files, HTTP serves web pages and ARP maps IP addresses to MAC addresses.'),
('a52ee741-04b5-418e-807b-d55ee86b4467', 'A 2D array with 3 rows and 4 columns holds 3 × 4 = 12 elements. The 7 option is 3 + 4, which adds the dimensions rather than multiplying them.'),
('a68d4eeb-8da2-4cda-8ca7-d718c3e68ab6', 'The area under a velocity–time graph gives displacement. The triangle has base 10 s and height 20 m s⁻¹, so the area is ½ × 10 × 20 = 100 m. The 200 m option forgets the one-half.'),
('a78eeee0-7359-47e5-a8fe-b0e8305142cf', 'The integral of 1/x is the n = −1 case of the power rule, which fails there, giving ln|x| + c instead. The absolute value makes the result valid for negative x as well.'),
('a7e4096d-1f57-42d1-b8dc-56cec82c27d2', 'The number of permutations is ⁿPᵣ = n!/(n − r)!, so ⁸P₃ = 8!/5! = 8 × 7 × 6 = 336. The 56 option is ⁸C₃, which ignores the order of selection.'),
('a877ceba-fd6e-4284-972e-3800ddde0237', 'Rearrange the identity sec²θ = 1 + tan²θ by subtracting tan²θ from both sides, which gives sec²θ − tan²θ = 1.'),
('a8928a03-6357-4fed-a654-fd107c557383', 'The standard CD sampling rate is 44 100 samples per second, the figure fixed by the Red Book audio CD standard. The other rates are used for different applications.'),
('a92ad44b-497a-4357-be48-cce823efd860', 'The graph of |x − 2| is the graph of x − 2 with the negative part reflected upwards. The vertex is where x − 2 = 0, so x = 2 and y = 0, giving (2, 0).'),
('a934bfd3-9336-4f12-a0da-2efbda85eac8', 'Frequency is the reciprocal of period: f = 1 ÷ T = 1 ÷ 0.020 s = 50 Hz. The 0.02 Hz option is the period itself, not the frequency.'),
('aab6da24-c23c-41e1-a98b-9e92beeb3984', 'For ax² + bx + c = 0 the sum of the roots is −b/a = −(−9)/3 = 3, and the product is c/a = 2/3. The 2/3 option is the product, not the sum.'),
('aad90d6b-3073-41a2-91ba-c41b582fe437', 'Electric field strength is E = F ÷ Q = 0.02 N ÷ (5 × 10⁻⁶ C) = 4000 N C⁻¹. Field strength is force divided by charge, so multiplying the two quantities is the wrong operation.'),
('ac97c994-7700-498a-8fff-b113a0bd78cb', 'The weight mg acts vertically down. Resolving along the slope, the component of weight parallel to the slope is mg sin θ, while the perpendicular component is mg cos θ.'),
('aca3661c-e0e3-4bfe-ab34-b9116e504ab1', 'Wave speed is v = fλ = 50 Hz × 6.0 m = 300 m s⁻¹. The 8.3 m s⁻¹ option is f ÷ λ, which gives the wrong units for a speed.')
) as v(id, e)
where q.id = v.id::uuid;
